            <ArticleTitle>Angiographic observations 10 years following coronary laser balloon angioplasty.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>357-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient underwent laser balloon angioplasty (LBA) combined with local intracoronary heparin therapy for treatment of a high grade stenosis of the mid-portion of the left anterior descending (LAD) coronary artery. Sustained patency of the LBA-treated lesion and no new coronary stenoses were found in a 10-year angiographic follow-up study.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>(J Interven Cardiol 2005;18:357-360).</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
